WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.160
Open the Sikh scripture,
the Guru Granth Sahib,

2
00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:05.140
and you find a surprise.

3
00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:09.410
Beside the Gurus' hymns sit hymns
by saints who were not Sikhs,

4
00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:12.640
including a Muslim Sufi, Sheikh Farid.

5
00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:15.670
Sikhs bow daily before their words.

6
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.640
Guru Nanak was born into a Hindu family.

7
00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:23.060
He met Hindu priests, Muslim
judges and wandering yogis.

8
00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:26.320
So when Guru Nanak met
them, did he come to argue,

9
00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:27.720
or to listen?

10
00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:32.410
In this mission, you'll read what the
scripture itself says about other religions.

11
00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:35.050
Then you'll trace the
pattern in his meetings,

12
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.020
and weigh up what they
show about other religions.

13
00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:42.840
Your mission: find out whether Guru
Nanak came to argue or to listen.
